        bullets: [
          `The tutorial (trainer page /tutorial; participants follow the trainer and the slides): Figma → MCP → token-exact code in 4 steps (5 min frame, 15 min steps with the room)`,
          `Participants prompt Claude in the cohort's framework along exactly that guide: compose a ${TARGET.name} from ${TARGET.parts} — no change to an existing component API, but composition from existing building blocks (35 min generation, 10:25–11:00)`,
          'Important: do not type the code yourself, prompt it',
          'Ladder stage 2, the agent checks itself (10 min, 11:00–11:10, one pass, golden prompts §1a): the agent runs `npm run lint` and `npm run build`, reports each exit code and repairs from the output (the full log when the summary has no error text). Then break it on purpose: add an `<img src="/avatar.png">` without `alt` and a `<div (click)="save()">Save</div>` to the Settings Card, do not fix anything, run lint and report the exit code and the rule ids. Then repair from the lint output and read the repair: did the agent write `alt=""`? Green is not right. Last, remove the image and the div again and run both checks. If the agent stalls, type the command yourself',
