          'Missing in the file: what the agent guesses (15 min, two slides). Each row of the readiness checklist, Part A, read as "missing, so the agent guesses this": a value not bound to a variable means the literal lands in code, a code name that cannot be recovered is guessed, no Auto Layout means padding and gap guessed from pixel offsets, default layer names become a tree of anonymous divs. The pink test and the linter have just shown the first row on a real master; the other rows are said, not demonstrated',
          'The readiness checklist (trainer source: /readiness) for one Atelier master: the linter and the pink test answer the rows on tokens, names and instances, the remaining rows are filled in by looking (10 min). The second form, for your own file, is a handout (`workshop/handouts/figma-readiness-checklist.md`); Day 2 Block 05 starts it',
