        ],
        stretch:
          'Pick the check that failed most often on the Atelier master and write the one-line fix a designer could apply in ten minutes. The same checks for your own file are in the readiness handout (`workshop/handouts/figma-readiness-checklist.md`).',
        recap:
          'Which of the checks would have stopped the AI from guessing on this master?',
        trainer: [
          'Everyone runs the linter twice on `Inputs/AtlButton` (node `129:20`) in the duplicate; both prompts are on `course/figma-pruefen.md`. First with three rules: exactly three findings, all real. Then with every rule: 23 findings when measured on the planted duplicate on 2026-11-21 (19 on an unplanted file), 18 of them "critical" contrast failures on the label inside the hidden `_disabled-overlay` (the false alarm), one about Auto Layout on the set (a matter of opinion) and the planted empty `Icon/Arrow` frame a second time; the count moves with the file, so run it once before the session. "A finding is something to sort, not a verdict." The linter does not see whether the design is right, nor spacing and radius.',
          'The three-rule run on the duplicate returns exactly three findings, one per rule, all real (a colour variable unbound with the same hex, a layer named `Frame 12`, a hidden empty `Icon/Arrow` frame): the answer key and the planting snippet are in golden prompts §1c. UNVERIFIED (rehearse: R-040): whether 10 minutes are enough for the remaining checklist rows.',
        ],
      },
      {
        num: '04',
        time: '14:15–15:30 · 75 min',
        title: 'Guardrails: stories as claims, and MCP',
