          "What carries your docs, and what you depend on (5 min, talk only, no exercise): the Storybook MCP on your own Storybook is the route that brings your design system's docs to the agents of the teams that consume it; the Figma linter, the accessibility audit and the parity check all stand on the third-party figma-console-mcp, a dependency you choose",
          "The second route to Figma (10 min, an exercise): Figma's own MCP server joins your seat with one command (`claude mcp add --transport http figma https://mcp.figma.com/mcp`), a login under `/mcp` and one question for the design context of your own component; then compare the answer with your code, element and states. It complements figma-console-mcp, it does not replace it: design context and a code template there, the checks here. The answer is a template to translate, not code to check in",
          "Transfer (15 min, a self-assessment): the scorecard (`workshop/handouts/ds-scorecard.md`) is the frame. From memory, because the course machines are Conciso's and nobody has their own system open: mark its seven rows for your own design system (yes / partly / no), pick the weakest row and write your next step for it; the exit round reads it out. Homework, not room work: run both checklists with the check prompt on your own system, the Figma checklist (`workshop/handouts/figma-readiness-checklist.md`) and the Storybook checklist (`workshop/handouts/storybook-readiness-checklist.md`; it includes the read-only self-check prompt), each time-boxed at 30 minutes. Nobody starts a checklist in the room",
          'Outlook: productive use in your own repo; the anatomy above is the checklist. Outcomes are named "component and stories"; the proof line stays `/verify`',
        ],
        trainer: [
          'Transfer slide, one conditional bullet: "A designer without an agent: a lint plugin in Figma (FigmaLint)". TODO(owner): keep it only once a run without an API key has shown what it does.',
          'TODO(owner): how a participant\'s workspace leaves the course machine (ADR-0178 leaves it open). Until the owner decides, the material says only "the trainer tells you how".',
          "Exercise with Figma's own MCP server: asked from an Angular workspace, the server answered with React and Tailwind for the AtlButton master (one call, measured 2026-11-21; ADR-0190). Not rehearsed on a seat: the login, which server the agent picks with both connected, the answer for a participant's own component.",
        ],
        stretch:
          'Draft the three guiding principles you would write for your own design system.',
        recap:
          'Exit round: one sentence each — the first thing you will do in your own design system next week.',
      },
    ],
  },
];

// Plain strings with `backticks` become <code>; everything else is escaped.
const md = inlineMd;

const dayId = (d: Day) => `day-${d.day.replace(' ', '-').toLowerCase()}`;
const blockId = (d: Day, b: Block) =>
  `day-${d.day.replace(/\D/g, '')}-block-${b.num}`;
const dayToc = (d: Day) => [
  { id: dayId(d), label: d.day },
  ...d.blocks.map((b) => ({ id: blockId(d, b), label: `${b.num} ${b.title}` })),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="2-Day Training"
  description="Curriculum for the Atelier 2-day training — an AI-assisted design-to-code workflow with Figma, Storybook, MCP and Claude Code. Angular by default, other frameworks on request, one framework per cohort."
  currentPath="/schulung"
  tocItems={[
    { id: 'audience', label: 'Audience' },
    { id: 'main-goal', label: 'Main goal' },
    { id: 'format', label: 'Format per day' },
    ...DAYS.flatMap(dayToc),
    { id: 'verify-title', label: 'Success verification' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="docs-inline-page">
    <PageHero
      time="2 days · 09:00–17:30 each (6 h 50 min net)"
      title="2-Day Training"
      ledeMax="640px"
    >
      An AI-assisted design-to-code workflow for developers with a solid
      frontend background. The default framework is Angular; other frameworks
      are possible on request, with one framework per cohort. At the end there
      is a <strong>self-designed and implemented component</strong> in Figma,
      Storybook and code.
    </PageHero>

    <Callout tone="note" title="For instructors">
      <p>
        This page is the two-day training curriculum, aimed at instructors
        planning a cohort. Participants cannot open this site: they work from
        the slides, the printed handouts and the workspace's
        <code>course/</code> folder (ADR-0184). The pages named below are the
        trainer's reference. Day 1 starts at
        <a href="/workshop" class="docs-link-primary">Setup</a>, and Day 2 has
        its own page,
        <a href="/build-your-own" class="docs-link-primary">Build your own</a>.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    <div class="objective-box">
      <div class="objective-col">
        <h2 id="audience" class="objective-heading objective-heading--accent">
          Audience
        </h2>
        <ul class="objective-list">
          <li>Developers with a frontend background</li>
          <li>Little experience with Figma, Storybook, MCP or AI codegen</li>
          <li>Up to 8 participants per cohort</li>
          <li>
            Cohort language: German. The material (docs, Storybook, briefs,
            prompts) is in English throughout — reading comprehension is assumed
          </li>
          <li>
            Angular by default; another framework on request, one framework per
            cohort — the code is secondary
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="objective-col">
        <h2 id="main-goal" class="objective-heading">Main goal</h2>
        <ul class="objective-list objective-list--muted">
          <li>
            Understand the four pillars: Figma · Storybook · MCP · Claude Code
          </li>
          <li>Master the end-to-end design-to-code workflow</li>
          <li>Prompt a component from Figma spec to production code</li>
          <li>Apply the a11y and dark-mode loop with confidence</li>
          <li>Carry the loop over to your own design system</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="format">
      <Callout tone="tip" title="Format per day">
        <p>
          6 h 50 min net, 09:00–17:30 · 60 min lunch · 2× 15 min coffee breaks ·
          10 min buffer. The machines are provisioned by Conciso before Day 1
          (owner decision 2026-11-12, ADR-0178); what a provisioned machine has
          is listed in ADR-0178. Nothing is installed in the room and nothing is
          mailed beforehand. To set up your own machine, see
          <a href="/workshop" class="docs-link-primary">Workshop Setup</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every block has the same shape: why it exists, the docs pages it uses,
          what everyone has when it is done, what to do, a stretch task for fast
          finishers, and a recap. Trainer notes are marked as such.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </div>

    {DAYS.map((day) => <section
      class="schulung-day"
      aria-labelledby={dayId(day)}
    >
      <header class="schulung-day-header">
        <span class="schulung-day-eyebrow">{day.day}</span>
        <h2 class="schulung-day-title" id={dayId(day)}>
          {day.title}
        </h2>
        <p class="schulung-day-goal"><strong>Day goal:</strong> {day.goal}</p>
      </header>

      <ol class="docs-step-list schulung-blocks">
        {day.blocks.map((block) => <li
          id={blockId(day, block)}
          class={`docs-step-row schulung-block${block.risk ? ' schulung-block--risk' : ''}`}
        >
          <span class="docs-step-badge">{block.num}</span>
          <div>
            <div class="schulung-block-meta">
              <span class="schulung-block-time">{block.time}</span>
              <span class="schulung-block-format">{block.format}</span>
              {block.risk && <span class="schulung-block-risk">High-risk</span>}
            </div>
            <h3 class="docs-h3">{block.title}</h3>
            <dl class="schulung-fields">
              <div>
                <dt>Why</dt>
                <dd>{block.why}</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>Pages</dt>
                <dd>
                  {block.pages.map((p, i) => (
                    <>
                      {i > 0 && ', '}
                      <a href={p.href} class="docs-link-primary">{p.label}</a>
                    </>
                  ))}
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>Done when</dt>
                <dd set:html={md(block.done)} />
              </div>
            </dl>
            <ul class="schulung-bullets">
              {block.bullets.map((b) => (
                <li set:html={md(b)} />
              ))}
            </ul>
            <dl class="schulung-fields schulung-fields--after">
              {block.stretch && <div>
                <dt>Stretch</dt>
                <dd set:html={md(block.stretch)} />
              </div>}
              {block.recap && <div>
                <dt>Recap</dt>
                <dd set:html={md(block.recap)} />
              </div>}
              {block.trainer &&
                block.trainer.map((t) => <div class="schulung-trainer">
                  <dt>Trainer note</dt>
                  <dd set:html={md(t)} />
                </div>)}
            </dl>
          </div>
        </li>)}
      </ol>

      <div class="schulung-result">
        <h3 class="schulung-result-heading">Deliverable per participant</h3>
        <ul class="objective-list">
          {day.result.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>)}

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="verify-title">
      <h2 class="docs-section-title" id="verify-title">Success verification</h2>
      <p
        style="
          color: var(--ui-color-text-muted);
          line-height: 1.6;
          margin-bottom: 1rem;
        "
      >
        End-to-end check per participant at the end of Day 2: five outcomes,
        then one proof line. Since ADR-0137 everyone works in their own
        generated workspace, so the gates there belong to their own work: red
        means red, not "red by design". The earlier note about three expectedly
        red gates (<code>check:sync</code>, <code>check:a11y-parity</code>,
        <code>check:design-status</code>) applied to the clone and no longer
        holds — it was a side effect of participants working in <em>our</em>
        repo.
      </p>
      <ol class="schulung-verify">
        {DAY2_DONE.map((item) => (
          <li set:html={inlineMd(item)} />
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <HelpFooter page="schulung" />

    <BottomNav
      items={[
        { to: '/', label: 'Prev', title: 'Overview', icon: 'dashboard' },
        {
          to: '/workshop',
          label: 'Next',
          title: 'Setup',
          icon: 'build_circle',
        },
      ]}
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .schulung-fields {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.6rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    font-size: var(--ui-font-size-sm);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .schulung-fields--after {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
  }
  .schulung-fields > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 6.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .schulung-fields dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: var(--ui-font-size-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ui-color-text-muted);
    padding-top: 0.1rem;
  }
  .schulung-fields dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ui-color-text);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .schulung-trainer dt {
    color: var(--ui-color-danger);
  }
  .schulung-fields code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--ui-color-primary);
    background: var(--ui-color-primary-light);
    padding: 0.05em 0.35em;
    border-radius: var(--ui-radius-sm);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .schulung-fields > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.1rem;
    }
  }
  .schulung-day {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }
  .schulung-day + .schulung-day {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ui-color-border);
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .schulung-day-header {
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }
  .schulung-day-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: var(--ui-font-size-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ui-color-primary);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ui-color-primary) 12%, transparent);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }
  .schulung-day-title {
    font-size: var(--ui-font-size-2xl);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
    color: var(--ui-color-text);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .schulung-day-goal {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ui-color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--ui-font-size-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 60rem;
  }
  .schulung-day-goal strong {
    color: var(--ui-color-text);
  }

  .schulung-blocks {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .schulung-block-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
    font-size: var(--ui-font-size-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    color: var(--ui-color-text-muted);
  }
  .schulung-block-time {
    color: var(--ui-color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .schulung-block-format {
    color: var(--ui-color-text-muted);
  }
  .schulung-block-format::before {
    content: '·';
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .schulung-block-risk {
    color: var(--ui-color-danger);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .schulung-block-risk::before {
    content: '·';
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
    opacity: 0.5;
    color: var(--ui-color-text-muted);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .schulung-block--risk .docs-step-badge {
    color: var(--ui-color-danger);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ui-color-danger) 12%, transparent);
  }

  .schulung-bullets {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-size: var(--ui-font-size-md);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ui-color-text);
  }
  .schulung-bullets li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .schulung-bullets li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.6em;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ui-color-primary);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .schulung-bullets code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--ui-color-primary);
    background: var(--ui-color-primary-light);
    padding: 0.05em 0.35em;
    border-radius: var(--ui-radius-sm);
  }

  .schulung-result {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem;
    background: var(--ui-color-surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--ui-color-border);
    border-radius: var(--ui-radius-md);
  }
  .schulung-result-heading {
    margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
    font-size: var(--ui-font-size-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ui-color-success);
  }

  .schulung-verify {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--ui-font-size-md);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ui-color-text);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  /* The items are set:html strings, so Astro's scope attribute never reaches
   * their <code> elements — hence :global. */
  .schulung-verify :global(code) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--ui-color-primary);
    background: var(--ui-color-primary-light);
    padding: 0.05em 0.35em;
    border-radius: var(--ui-radius-sm);
  }
</style>
